From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 14:46:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 67/75] fix(gastown): report lost work before the child gate in
 polecat-home-audit (gcp-fzjo)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The child gate ran before the two lost-work report gates and short-circuited
the rest of the loop, so a home hosting any per-bead worktree was never
inspected for uncommitted paths or unpublished commits. Its justifying comment
— "the per-bead reaper owns children; once it has cleared them the home becomes
eligible" — does not hold: the reaper runs dry-run today (the witness passes no
--no-dry-run), and even at full strength a child kept for a legitimately open
bead masks its parent home's report for that child's whole lifetime. The
masking is self-sustaining: a home with children is the home that has been
doing work, and the gate re-fires every cycle for as long as the children live.

Live proof at filing: gastown.nux emitted home_dirty_kept on 2026-08-27 and
08-28, then went silent the moment children appeared, with the same uncommitted
path still on disk. On gascity the sweep reported nothing for gastown.furiosa,
which a hand scan found detached with 61 uncommitted paths.

The two verdicts are independent facts, not competing ones, so neither
short-circuits the other now. Gates 3a/3b (dirty, unpublished) are evaluated
for every home and record their verdicts; gate 4 (children, THE TRAP) follows
and records its own. Each sets a KEEP flag rather than skipping the loop, and a
single skip after the gates counts the home once — so a home kept for two
reasons logs both lines and still reports skipped=1. Gate 4 keeps governing
removal exactly as before: it now suppresses the teardown and nothing else.
The unreadable paths (git status / rev-list failed or cut short by the budget)
still abandon the home immediately, because nothing further can be established
about a checkout git cannot read.

Flipping the reaper to --no-dry-run is a separate rollout decision and does not
substitute for this: the ordering coupled lost-work reporting to unrelated
per-bead state.

Validation: new test_a_home_with_children_is_still_reported_for_lost_work
covers both masked shapes (dirty behind a child, unpushed behind a child),
asserts both verdicts are emitted, asserts THE TRAP still defers teardown, and
asserts the summary counts each home once. Verified red against the pre-fix
script ("the dirt in a home with children was never reported") and green after.
Full gastown shell suite, go vet/build/test, golangci-lint and
validate_registry all clean. mol-witness-patrol's verdict table is updated so
home_children_kept no longer reads as a statement about the home's contents.
