@@ -692,7 +692,7 @@ tail -n 50 "${LOG_DIR:-$GC_CITY/.gc/runtime/logs}/polecat-home-audit.log" | jq -
 | `home_removal_pending` | Passed every gate; dry-run, so NOT removed | Routine while the rollout is staged — this is the would-remove set to review |
 | `home_removed` | Removed. Routine, and only once `--no-dry-run` is wired | Log only. `worktree-setup.sh` recreates the home when the slot next spawns |
 | `home_removal_failed` | The directory survived removal | Investigate permissions or mounts, mail the mayor — same as `worktree_reap_failed` above |
-| `home_children_kept` | The home holds per-bead worktrees, so removing it would take them too | None — expected. The reaper clears children first; the home becomes eligible on a later cycle |
+| `home_children_kept` | The home holds per-bead worktrees, so removing it would take them too | None on its own — expected. The reaper clears children first; the home becomes eligible on a later cycle. It defers TEARDOWN only and says nothing about the home's contents, so read it alongside any `home_dirty_kept` / `home_unpublished_commits_kept` line for the same agent — one home can carry both |
 | `home_dirty_kept` | Uncommitted work in a home nothing owns | **This is the failure this step exists to prevent.** A respawned namepool slot inherits it and fails submit-and-exit's clean-state check (gascity-vst). Salvage or clear it by hand |
 | `home_unpublished_commits_kept` | Commits reaching no remote, often on a detached HEAD | Investigate by hand. Whether they are superseded takes a CONTENT check at origin — a rebase/squash-merging refinery rewrites hashes, so `git merge-base --is-ancestor` lies here. The sweep deliberately does not guess |
 | `home_owner_unconfirmed` | The roster parsed but this home's liveness query did not answer | Nothing was removed. If it repeats, the roster shape has drifted |
